- correctness bugs in the changed code itself (wrong condition, state left inconsistent, double save, a throw inside a destructor or across a C callback, a rethrow `throw;` used outside an active catch).

Report only findings you can point to a file and line for, most severe first, each with a concrete scenario (inputs or state, then wrong outcome). Say plainly when you found nothing in an area. Under 600 words.

